unimodal locus) and <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0036/" title="(P6): the collapse identity and the period-6 structure" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0036/" display-uri="ffi-0036" type="local">(P6)</fr:link> (the collapse identity and the
period-6 structure).</html:p>
            <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0030/" title="z_u(c) and the modality formula" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0030/" display-uri="ffi-0030" type="local">z_u(c) and the modality formula</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0032/" title="The graded count for z_u (H4)" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0032/" display-uri="ffi-0032" type="local">The graded count for z_u (H4)</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0034/" title="(P4): the maximum of umod over compositions" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0034/" display-uri="ffi-0034" type="local">(P4): the maximum of umod over compositions</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0035/" title="(P5): the grand formula off the unimodal locus" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0035/" display-uri="ffi-0035" type="local">(P5): the grand formula off the unimodal locus</fr:link>,
<fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0036/" title="(P6): the collapse identity and the period-6 structure" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0036/" display-uri="ffi-0036" type="local">(P6): the collapse identity and the period-6 structure</fr:link>.</html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors />
            <fr:uri>https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0045/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>ffi-0045</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/ffi/ffi-0045/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="(NS): the strict/centralizer inequality">(NS): the strict/centralizer inequality</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>conjecture</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="area">frontier</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="thread">ns</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="status">open</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="provenance">scratch_nineteenth.md Result 13, items 15(e)--(f); result13_addendum.md; instruments ns_*.sage, mb_*.sage.</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>(NS). <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
  N_{\mathrm {strict}} \le  N_z,
]]></fr:tex>
where <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[N_{\mathrm {strict}}]]></fr:tex> is the nullity of the pairing on honest strict
Hom-triples and <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[N_z]]></fr:tex> the centralizer-side count.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Role in the skeleton.</html:strong> This is the sole residue of the whole chain. By the exact ledger
<fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0046/" title="The Fredholm ledger" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0046/" display-uri="ffi-0046" type="local">the Fredholm ledger</fr:link>, multi-block <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0043/" title="Lemma V" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0043/" display-uri="ffi-0043" type="local">Lemma V</fr:link> follows
from it; and <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0043/" title="Lemma V" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0043/" display-uri="ffi-0043" type="local">Lemma V</fr:link> is the last open input to
<fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0035/" title="(P5): the grand formula off the unimodal locus" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0035/" display-uri="ffi-0035" type="local">(P5)</fr:link>, hence to <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0033/" title="(Deg-Opt): the grand formula for umod" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0033/" display-uri="ffi-0033" type="local">(Deg-Opt)</fr:link>. Everything else in the
growth program is proven.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Status.</html:strong> Measured with equality, <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[N_{\mathrm {strict}} = N_z]]></fr:tex>, 13/13 (mb_dual.sage).
Two independent reductions exist and neither has closed it:
<fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0047/" title="(Q-MOD): the reductive repair" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0047/" display-uri="ffi-0047" type="local">(Q-MOD)</fr:link> and <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0048/" title="The peeling induction" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0048/" display-uri="ffi-0048" type="local">the peeling induction</fr:link>.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Warning.</html:strong> ns_elim_defs.sage as committed is the pre-fix draft. Measure
(NS) only through ns_clean.sage or mb_dual.sage until it is
repaired.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0042/" title="Splits, flanks, tallness" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0042/" display-uri="ffi-0042" type="local">Splits, flanks, tallness</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0043/" title="Lemma V" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0043/" display-uri="ffi-0043" type="local">Lemma V</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0046/" title="The Fredholm ledger" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0046/" display-uri="ffi-0046" type="local">The Fredholm ledger</fr:link>.</html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors />
            <fr:uri>https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0043/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>ffi-0043</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/ffi/ffi-0043/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="Lemma V">Lemma V</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>lemma</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="area">frontier</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="thread">ns</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="status">refuted</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="provenance">result13_addendum.md; certificates p5_vtprime (EQUALITY), p5_lemmaV_asym; p5_vt_check's "FAILURES" line reports the superseded condition only.</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>Lemma V, as originally stated: for a split
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[c = (c_L, v, c_R)]]></fr:tex> with reductive quotient data
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[c']]></fr:tex>, <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
  z_u(c) \le  z_u(c') + v^2.
]]></fr:tex></html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Status.</html:strong> <html:strong>False as stated</html:strong> over all splits: 958 counterexample
splits in umod_tables.tsv at <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n \le  12]]></fr:tex>. The smallest is
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[c = (1,2,3,1)]]></fr:tex> split as <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[(1) \mid  (2) \mid  (3,1)]]></fr:tex>, where
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[11 > 6 + 4]]></fr:tex>.</html:p>
            <html:p>Two regimes survive and are proven. All 3-block splits <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[(a, v, b)]]></fr:tex> —
H17<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[']]></fr:tex>, five sub-lemmas: <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\sigma ]]></fr:tex>-avoidance (V-t<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[']]></fr:tex>) giving
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\dim  K \le  z']]></fr:tex> with equality; the decomposition
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[K = x_{XY} \oplus  K_0]]></fr:tex>; and a quotient-restriction injection into
intertwiners whose kernel is killed by the
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\binom {v}{2} + \binom {v}{2}]]></fr:tex> against <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[v^2]]></fr:tex> count, with
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\text {intw} = \binom {|a-b|}{2}]]></fr:tex>. And the tall regime,
<fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0044/" title="Tall-Lemma V" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0044/" display-uri="ffi-0044" type="local">Tall-Lemma V</fr:link>.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Warning.</html:strong> The old condition (V-t) <html:em>fails</html:em> when <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[|a - b| \ge  2]]></fr:tex>, at
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\binom {|a-b|}{2}]]></fr:tex>; (V-t<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[']]></fr:tex>) is its repair. (V-t<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[']]></fr:tex>) is itself false
in the multi-block setting, and <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {V}_0 \le  v^2]]></fr:tex> holds only for
the <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathfrak {k}]]></fr:tex>-version.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:em>Superseded by:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0044/" title="Tall-Lemma V" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0044/" display-uri="ffi-0044" type="local">Tall-Lemma V</fr:link> for the tall regime; <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0045/" title="(NS): the strict/centralizer inequality" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0045/" display-uri="ffi-0045" type="local">(NS): the strict/centralizer inequality</fr:link> for the
general case.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0030/" title="z_u(c) and the modality formula" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0030/" display-uri="ffi-0030" type="local">z_u(c) and the modality formula</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0042/" title="Splits, flanks, tallness" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0042/" display-uri="ffi-0042" type="local">Splits, flanks, tallness</fr:link>.</html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors />
            <fr:uri>https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0030/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>ffi-0030</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/ffi/ffi-0030/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="z_u(c) and the modality formula">z_u(c) and the modality formula</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>definition</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="area">growth</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="provenance">lc_law.md; journal sec:zu.</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>Fix a composition <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[c = (c_1, \dots , c_\ell )]]></fr:tex> of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n]]></fr:tex> and let
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[y \in  \mathfrak {n}_{c}]]></fr:tex> be <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[B]]></fr:tex>-generic. Write <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
  z_u(c) = \dim (\mathfrak {z}(y) \cap  \mathfrak {u}),
]]></fr:tex>
the dimension of the centralizer of a generic element inside the upper
triangular nilpotent Lie algebra.</html:p>
            <html:p>For parabolic slices the modality is then <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
  \operatorname {umod}(\mathfrak {n}_{c}) = d_c - \frac {n(n - 1)}{2} + z_u(c),
  \qquad  d_c = \sum _i c_i^2 - n,
]]></fr:tex>
where <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[d_c]]></fr:tex> adjusts the flag count. So computing <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\operatorname {umod}(\mathfrak {n}_{c})]]></fr:tex>
is computing <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[z_u(c)]]></fr:tex>, which is what <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0032/" title="The graded count for z_u (H4)" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0032/" display-uri="ffi-0032" type="local">the graded count</fr:link>
does.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0028/" title="U-modality" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0028/" display-uri="ffi-0028" type="local">U-modality</fr:link>.</html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
